userStories.description:
**Goal** — Replace whole-file job log reads with a reverse chunked line reader and make the job panel request the last non-empty lines.

**Motivation** — A log ending in 12 informative lines followed by 12 blank lines showed none, although the panel contract calls for the last 12 non-empty lines.

**Approach** — Target: `logTail(id: string, lines?: number, opts?: { readonly nonEmpty?: boolean }): Promise<string>`. It delegates to a new `readTailLines(path, lines, { nonEmpty })` in a new file `packages/nax/src/chat/jobs/log-tail.ts`. The raw-line result is unchanged for callers without the option (`jobs-provider.ts`, `useChatPicker.ts`): the last N lines, a single trailing line break ignored, `\r\n` treated as a break, `""` for a non-finite `lines`, for `lines < 1` (after flooring a fractional value), for a missing file or for an unknown id. With `nonEmpty: true` the result is the last N lines whose trimmed text is non-empty, returned as their original text (a trailing `\r` stripped, no other trimming), joined with `\n`. `readTailLines` returns `""` when `size` or `readRange` reports `ENOENT`; `Bun.file(path).size` of a missing file (0) also yields `""`. `_jobRunnerDeps.readLog` is replaced by `_logTailDeps` in `log-tail.ts`: `size(path): Promise<number>` and `readRange(path, start, end): Promise<Uint8Array>`, the seam tests count bytes through.

`readTailLines` (new, `packages/nax/src/chat/jobs/log-tail.ts`). Reads backward from the end of the file in chunks of `LOG_TAIL_CHUNK_BYTES` (64 KiB), splitting on a local `NEWLINE_BYTE` constant (10) before decoding (so a multi-byte UTF-8 character is never cut), and stops as soon as it holds N qualifying lines plus one line break before them, or reaches the start of the file. Worked skeleton:

```ts
export const LOG_TAIL_CHUNK_BYTES = 64 * 1024;
export async function readTailLines(path: string, lines: number, opts: { readonly nonEmpty?: boolean } = {}): Promise<string> {
  // size = await _logTailDeps.size(path); end = size; carry = empty bytes
  // while end > 0 and collected < lines:
  //   start = max(0, end - LOG_TAIL_CHUNK_BYTES); chunk = await _logTailDeps.readRange(path, start, end)
  //   bytes = chunk + carry; split at NEWLINE_BYTE; the first piece becomes the new carry unless start === 0
  //   decode the complete pieces, strip a trailing "\r", walk them last-to-first, keep the ones that qualify
  //   end = start
  // return the kept lines in file order joined with "\n"
}
```

`logTailSource` (`packages/nax/src/chat/jobs/job-panel-view.ts`). Target: `jobs.logTail(job.id, JOB_PANEL_LOG_LINES, { nonEmpty: true })`. The `Pick<ChatJobs, "logTail">` parameter type follows the new signature.

Symbols this feature only reads: `logLinesOf(logTail)` (trims, drops empty lines, keeps the last `JOB_PANEL_LOG_LINES`). Unchanged. `readLogTail(path)`, a byte-bounded tail read with a newline-boundary rule, as a pattern; it is not reused because it bounds bytes, not lines.

Failure handling: The log file is missing when `logTail` runs: `""`, as today. `readRange` or `size` throws any other error: The error propagates, as `readLog` errors do today; `logTailSource` turns it into `""` for the panel.

Create `packages/nax/src/chat/jobs/log-tail.ts` — `readTailLines`, `LOG_TAIL_CHUNK_BYTES`, `_logTailDeps`; `packages/nax/test/unit/chat/jobs/log-tail.test.ts` — `readTailLines` tests (direct readTailLines tests); and `packages/nax/test/unit/chat/jobs/job-runner-log-tail.test.ts` — `logTail` tests over a real `createJobRunner` with an attached job record and a temp `logPath`, as `job-runner-attach.test.ts` builds them (logTail and panel-read tests). Update `packages/nax/test/unit/chat/jobs/job-panel-view.test.ts` — the assertion that `logTail` was called with exactly `("run-1a2b3c4d", JOB_PANEL_LOG_LINES)` now sees a third argument. The invariant becomes: called with `"run-1a2b3c4d"`, `JOB_PANEL_LOG_LINES` and `{ nonEmpty: true }`. US-003's `readTailLines` is consumed by `DetachedJobs.logTail` in the same story; its ACs drive it through `logTail` and `readJobPanelView`.

**Scope** — In: the new reverse byte reader and seam, the optional ChatJobs/DetachedJobs argument and delegation, panel wiring, direct-reader and real-runner regressions, and the existing panel assertion update. Out: transcript-retention changes belong to US-001 and failed-ACP-resume integration belongs to US-002. Revising `.nax/features/chat-job-panel/spec.md` so its `readJobPanelView` paragraph names the `nonEmpty` read is a manual edit made with this spec; no story edits `.nax/`. US-003 only: the background-task log reader `readLogTail` in `task-registry.ts` keeps its byte-bounded behaviour. US-003 only: a `nonEmpty` read of a log that holds fewer qualifying lines than asked scans back to the start of the file; no byte cap is added for that case. US-003 only: the panel refresh cadence (`JOB_PANEL_REFRESH_MS`) is unchanged. US-003 only: a log line longer than the whole file's remaining bytes is returned whole, however long; no per-line length cap is added.

**Interface** — `logTail(id: string, lines?: number, opts?: { readonly nonEmpty?: boolean }): Promise<string>`; `export const LOG_TAIL_CHUNK_BYTES = 64 * 1024;`; `export async function readTailLines(path: string, lines: number, opts: { readonly nonEmpty?: boolean } = {}): Promise<string>`; `_logTailDeps`: `size(path): Promise<number>` and `readRange(path, start, end): Promise<Uint8Array>`. Keep the existing default `JOB_LOG_TAIL_LINES` (40).
